# Gradle
.gradle/
build/
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
!gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

# Android
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab
.cxx/

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Captured OBD logs (may contain VIN / location traces)
*.obdlog
captures/

# Probe logs pulled off the phone.
#
# Same reasoning as above: they carry the adapter's Bluetooth MAC, the
# odometer reading, and raw MS-CAN frames. Useful evidence, not something to
# publish. Findings belong in docs/; the raw files stay local.
# Probe and drive logs, including milestone sessions. See the note at the
# bottom of this file: a drive log is route data, and none of it is committed.
tools/probe-logs/*

# Android local SDK path (machine-specific)
local.properties

# Signing material. NEVER commit these.
#
# The upload keystore is the permanent identity of the app on Play: lose it
# and dev.swordfish can never be updated again under that package name.
# Back it up somewhere outside this repo (password manager / offline copy).
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties

# Logs pulled off the phone with `adb pull`.
#
# SAME REASONING as tools/probe-logs above, and worth stating separately
# because this directory did not exist when that rule was written.
#
# A drive log is a GPS trace of where the car has been -- which, for a car
# parked at home every night, is a home address with timestamps. The MS-CAN
# captures carry raw bus frames and the odometer. None of it belongs in a
# public repo, and `git add -A` must never be able to sweep it in.
#
# Findings go in docs/MSCAN_SIGNALS.md; the raw files stay on this machine.
logs/

# Layout harness output. Regenerated in a second by
# `./gradlew :layout-harness:run`; committing PNGs would bloat history for
# something derivable. The harness SOURCE is committed.
tools/layout-harness/out/

# Personal drafts. Kept on disk, out of the repo -- these are Frank's to
# publish or not, and a `git add -A` should not make that decision.
docs/REDDIT_POST_DRAFT*.md

# Personal prep and internal working notes. Kept on disk, out of the repo.
#
# These are about HOW THE WORK GETS PRESENTED, not about how it works:
# speaking notes, what to say if challenged, what not to overclaim, and
# session-to-session working state. None of it is useful to a reader of the
# project, and all of it is Frank's to publish or not.
#
# Project knowledge belongs in README.md and the topic docs
# (MSCAN_SIGNALS, VEHICLE_SURVEY, THE_JET_ANALOGY, ...). Keep the two apart.
docs/DEMO_SCRIPT.md
docs/demo-overlays.html
docs/SESSION_HANDOFF_*.md

# Kotlin incremental build state. Machine-local, not source.
.kotlin/

# Architecture and working notes for the AI assistant. Kept on disk, out of
# the repo: it is session-to-session working state, not project knowledge a
# reader needs, and it accumulates personal context by nature.
CLAUDE.md

# Raw drive captures and device logs. These are route data -- an altitude and
# speed trace over time reconstructs where the car went, and every capture
# starts and ends at home. Milestone notes belong in docs/ without the traces.
tools/probe-logs/
